---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Rethinking Business Strategy" description="Volume overview for Artificial Intelligence: Rethinking Business Strategy.">
  <section class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-4xl space-y-10 rounded-3xl bg-white/95 p-8 shadow-card sm:p-10">
    <header>
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-[#1b5ed8]">Overview</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-display font-semibold text-[#113e8c]">Artificial Intelligence: Rethinking Business Strategy</h1>
    </header>
    <article class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#113453]">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[#113e8c]">About this book</h2>
      <p>The world of business stands at a crossroads.</p>
      <p>
        While there is general agreement that its impact on business will resemble that of previous General Purpose Technologies like electricity or the internet, business leaders are overwhelmed by the noise around Artificial Intelligence and struggling to make complex decisions after the initial experimentation phases. Now is the time to identify which previously advocated strategic principles still hold when deciding on growth and innovation, and what are the relevant value drivers in the era of AI.
      </p>
      <p>
        <em>Artificial Intelligence: Rethinking Business Strategy</em> discusses how to use foresight techniques to help detect the signposts for future change and prepare for better exploitation of AI opportunities. It explores how to navigate the uncertainty about AI’s global regulation and supervision, standards and gatekeepers, speed of adoption and interrelated technological solutions as well as changes in geopolitical power dynamics. With the use of real-life examples, Teresa Martín-Retortillo defines plausible scenarios that will undoubtedly be a valuable compass for business leaders trying to distinguish noise from signals.
      </p>
      <p>
        Business and technical professionals in leadership positions, executives, product and project managers as well as policymakers will benefit immensely from this book’s exploration of future strategies that will hereon be required to generate sustainable value creation for businesses and for society.
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-3">
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-[#1b5ed8]"></span>
          <p class="text-lg leading-7 text-[#113453]">Thorough exploration of business strategy from classical foundations to the AI era</p>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-[#1b5ed8]"></span>
          <p class="text-lg leading-7 text-[#113453]">Practical concepts and frameworks designed to understand and implement AI-inspired strategies</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-8 text-[#113453]">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[#113e8c]">Author / Editor information</h2>
      <p>
        Teresa Martín-Retortillo is a senior executive with deep global experience in strategy and innovation, from executive boards to boards of directors of both private and listed companies. After two decades advising private equity investors and global corporations, she has spent the last decade executing different digital business models. She is a regular speaker at conferences and an engaging educator with over 30,000 followers of her online course.
      </p>
      <p>
        Her work at Goldman Sachs, Bain and Company, McGraw Hill Education and now at IE University as Executive President of Lifelong Learning and currently as SVP of Operations, has made her a sought after thought leader. She is a graduate of Harvard Business School.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Layout>
